                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "The system view only needs to indicate which chassis are present. Can we use a bitfield or a list indicating which chassis are present? For example, `m_presentChassisList = {\"chassis1\", \"chassis3\", \"chassis4\"};`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/thread_manager.hpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged. no need to keep JSON object as we can always gets it from configManager. updated with vector, as given the small bounded size of chassis entries, std::vector is efficient with direct chassis ID comparison here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/thread_manager.hpp",
                    "line": 77,
                    "reviewer": {
